{"name":"Paprika Kisses","hex":"#c24325","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paprika","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Powdered spice made from dried and ground fruits of sweet pepper (bell pepper) or chili pepper (cultivars of Capsicum annuum), or mixtures of these (used especially in Hungarian cooking).","A variety of the spice."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright reddish orange colour, like that of the dried paprika."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paprika"},{"term":"kisses","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of kiss","plural of kisse"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of kiss"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kisses"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paprika","blocks":[{"text":"Paprika is a spice made from dried and ground red peppers, Capsicum annuum. It is traditionally made from Capsicum annuum varietals in the Longum group, and while it can have varying levels of heat, the peppers used tend to be milder and have thinner flesh than those used to produce chili powder. The milder, sweet paprika is mainly composed of the fruit of the pepper with most of the seeds removed; whereas some seeds and stalks are retained in the peppers used for hotter paprika."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/Piment%C3%B3n_Tap_de_Cort%C3%AD_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paprika","wikidata":"Q3127593"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/1902-11-17%2C_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3n_Art%C3%ADstica%2C_Abriendo_el_pimiento%2C_Medina_Vera.jpg/500px-1902-11-17%2C_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3n_Art%C3%ADstica%2C_Abriendo_el_pimiento%2C_Medina_Vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/1902-11-17%2C_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3n_Art%C3%ADstica%2C_Abriendo_el_pimiento%2C_Medina_Vera.jpg/500px-1902-11-17%2C_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3n_Art%C3%ADstica%2C_Abriendo_el_pimiento%2C_Medina_Vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Opening the pepper, an illustration of Medina Vera","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1902-11-17%2C_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3n_Art%C3%ADstica%2C_Abriendo_el_pimiento%2C_Medina_Vera.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg/500px-Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg/1280px-Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg/500px-Paprika_Vendor_Budapest_big_hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&